-- the property the two-centre model enforces, stated without counting anything: any three atoms a bond
-- is incident on include two that are the same atom. Every bond of a molecule in the standard
-- representation has it, and a three-centre bond does not.
TwoCentred : HMol → Type 0
TwoCentred H = (i : hm-bonds H) → (x : hm-atoms H) → (y : hm-atoms H) → (z : hm-atoms H) → isTrue (hm-inc H i x) → isTrue (hm-inc H i y) → isTrue (hm-inc H i z) → Sum (x ≡ y) (Sum (y ≡ z) (x ≡ z))
